HST Office: upstream sc tests that print formulas expect the Calc A1 syntax; they now expect HST's Excel A1.

hst-sheets-excel-formula-conventions.patch makes Excel A1 the default UI formula syntax, so the expressions
that ScCondFormatHelper::GetExpression and ScConditionEntry::GetExpression print read Sheet1!$B2 and
Sheet2!$A$2 instead of $Sheet1.$B2 and $Sheet2.$A$2 (testTdf104026, testCondFormatImportCellIs,
testCondFormatExportCellIs). The references themselves are unchanged.

The same syntax prints imported formulas the Excel way: Comparison!$I:$J (testTdf131536), the intersection
operator as a space (testTdf160371), 'Новый.лист'!A1 (testNonAsciiWithDotXLSX), Calc's CEILING as CEILING.ODF
(testTdf143809) and external references as ['file://host/share/file.xlsx']Sheet1!A1:B5 (testTdf118990). These
failed identically in 1.0.2; only the printed syntax changes, values and references are still asserted as before.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: make CppunitTest_sc_cond_format CppunitTest_sc_subsequent_filters_test CppunitTest_sc_subsequent_filters_test2
CppunitTest_sc_subsequent_export_test2.
